6.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.14338,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":95.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ethan Allen Interiors Inc. operates as an interior design company, and manufacturer and retailer of home furnishings in the United States and internationally. The company operates through two segments: Wholesale and Retail. It offers case goods items, such as beds, dressers, armoires, tables, chairs, buffets, entertainment units, home office furniture, and wooden accents; upholstery comprising fabric-covered items, such as sleepers, recliners and other motion furniture, chairs, ottomans, custom pillows, sofas, loveseats, cut fabrics, and leather; and window treatments and drapery hardware, wall decors, florals, lighting, clocks, mattresses, bedspreads, throws, pillows, decorative accents, area rugs, flooring, wall coverings, and outdoor furnishings. The company also sells third-party furniture protection plans and sales less prompt payment discounts, sales allowances and other incentives. It markets and sells its products under the Ethan Allen brand through design centers, independent retailers, and other third parties as well as through ethanallen.com website. Ethan Allen Interiors Inc. was founded in 1932 and is headquartered in Danbury, Connecticut.","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $194K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $404 per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Ethan Allen Interiors Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $441M market cap on $579M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -10% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 55% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $41M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 11.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"News tone classified negative across 12 recent articles","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Ethan Allen Interiors Inc. (ETD) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/Precision_Trading_with_Ethan_Allen_Interiors_Inc._ETD_Risk_Zones_111126014802_1794379682.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794379682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Ethan Allen Interiors retreats 11% following earnings miss (ETD:NYSE)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669715-ethan-allen-interiors-retreats-11-following-earnings-miss","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794316769.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Ethan Allen Interiors declares $0.20 dividend (NYSE:ETD)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669462-ethan-allen-interiors-declares-0_20-dividend","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794283041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividen