air-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 11%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $16.23 to $22.77 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 14.3 vs 18.8 and P/FCF 10.6 vs 16.7 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 74% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 9.4% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 9.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The Street target $22.00 on average, 26% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 16% clears the cost of capital of 8.8% by 7pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.60).","It runs a 55% gross margin and converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.32x.","ROE of 8% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $15.7M.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.9, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.06).","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 1.5 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -9.9% over 3 years, -3.3% over 5 years and -3.1% over 10 years, so the decline is deepening.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -18.9% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 16%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (1.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 4, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 14.3%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 87%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (20 sales, net $1.1M sold).","It returns 11.6% a year to shareholders (1.1% in buybacks and 4.6% in dividends).","It pays out 128% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk.","Short interest is elevated at 11.4% of the float, 5.8 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,988 employees, each generates about $194K of revenue, 0.5x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $14K of free cash flow per employee.","Compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":74,"head":"Watch: composite 42, above the 39 line, but only 8% below fair value; it becomes a buy below $16.11.","pros":["Composite 42, above the 39 line (gates 15/25)","ROIC 15.9% vs WACC 8.8%","Net cash of $15.7M","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 14.3x vs sector 18.8x"],"cons":["Revenue shrank 3.3%/yr over 5y"],"flags":[],"need":["only 8% below fair value"],"buy_below":16.11,"vc":{"base":18.96,"base_src":"dcf","bear":16.23,"bull":22.77,"alt_median":19.02,"n_alt":3,"gap":-0.0033,"dispersion":0.1136,"level":"HIGH","why":[]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[14.64,15.51,16.23,16.72,17.06,17.41,17.81,18.14,18.43,18.7,18.99,19.37,19.67,20.02,20.44,20.83,21.37,21.88,22.77,23.9,27.05],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.687,"discount_rate":0.253,"terminal_growth":0.022,"exit_multiple":0.037},"ticker":"ETD","date":"2026-11-13"}